# Nested dynamic attrpath segment (D21, ported from pnix-clj's
# parse-attr-path/path->nested): a dynamic key can appear ANYWHERE in a
# dotted attrset-binding path, not just as a lone top-level key.
# `a.${x}.c = 2;` desugars to `a = { ${x} = { c = 2; }; };` -- a static
# sibling `a.b = 1;` under the same top-level key `a` still merges with it
# via merge_attr_field's dynamic-pairs fallback (oracle-verified against
# pnix-clj: `let x = "y"; in { a.b = 1; a.${x}.c = 2; }.a.y.c` => 2).
let x = "y"; in { a.b = 1; a.${x}.c = 2; }.a.y.c + { a.b = 1; a.${x}.c = 2; }.a.b
